{
  "_why": "Where every screenshot on this site comes from, so a screen that moved can be retaken instead of guessed at. The loop is in scripts/screenshots.mjs.",
  "instance": {
    "build": "CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -tags ee -o /tmp/meerkat-doc ./cmd/meerkat",
    "console": "the binary must EMBED the console, or the admin port answers a JSON status page: make ui first, or stage console/dist/console/browser into internal/admin/ui/dist",
    "edition": "Enterprise (-tags ee): the console's EE badges and the Enterprise screens are part of what is shown",
    "upstream": "node scripts/screenshots-upstream.mjs  (keeps running on 127.0.0.1:8099): the instance reaches the routes' services - http://docs:8080 and http://orders-api:8080, names of a stack - through it, as HTTP_PROXY; Billing is left out of the proxy on purpose (NO_PROXY), so the routes list shows a target that is down",
    "run": "HOSTNAME=meerkat-7d9f8c6b5-x2k4p MEERKAT_VERSION=1.0.1 HTTP_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8099 NO_PROXY=billing.svc.acme.internal MEERKAT_TENANCY=multi MEERKAT_ADMIN_PASSWORD=test1234 /tmp/meerkat-doc -addr :8086 -admin-addr 127.0.0.1:9096 -data /tmp/docdata",
    "seed": "node scripts/screenshots-seed.mjs  (once, on an EMPTY data directory)",
    "ports": "8086/9096 and 8087/9097 on purpose: this repository's own dev instance runs on 8082 and 9092 and must never be disturbed",
    "admin": "http://gateway.acme.example:9096",
    "data": "http://gateway.acme.example:8086",
    "signIn": "admin / test1234",
    "dataset": "Acme Corp (the primary organisation, renamed), its logo and tagline. Five routes, their services named as in a stack: Billing, Docs portal, Orders API, Inventory (maintenance), Catch-all. A role tree of nine roles with tags under three top-level roles, five accounts besides admin (one app admin, one infra admin), three groups (Finance, Front desk, Warehouse), a vault with two secrets and a value that routes use, a portal bar, two self-signed certificates and three TLS names, three control-plane tokens and two application tokens, two saved configurations, three schedules (a cadence, a cron line, one date), an OpenTelemetry collector at http://opentelemetry:4318, and the few updates the Audit caption describes. Orders API carries a deposited OpenAPI spec of 14 operations, five endpoint rules (a closed operation with a named exception, two role rules, two rate limits) and two audited operations. All in scripts/screenshots-seed.mjs.",
    "traffic": "the Metrics screen shows the last minute only: screenshots.mjs starts `screenshots-seed.mjs --traffic-only` itself for the shots marked traffic, and takes them last",
    "host": "gateway.acme.example: the name the browser is shown, mapped to 127.0.0.1 by Chromium (--host-resolver-rules), so no capture says localhost. The data plane listens on :8086 without an address, so the console derives the applications' origin from that name",
    "loopback": {
      "admin": "http://127.0.0.1:9096",
      "data": "http://127.0.0.1:8086",
      "why": "what the seed and the traffic use: Node resolves no made-up name"
    },
    "version": "MEERKAT_VERSION=1.0.1: the binary is built as dev, and the account menu and the release notes then read as a release, not as a development build"
  },
  "convert": "cwebp -quiet -q 82 -resize 1600 0 <shot>.png -o public/<file>  (done by screenshots.mjs --shoot)",
